hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"527","[AI-translation] Aisha (Raziallahu anha) se riwayat hai, unhon-ne kaha: Rasulullah (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) merey paas daakhil huey jabke merey paas do londiyaan Buas key geet gaa rahi thein. To Aap bistar par let gaey aur apna chehra pher liya. Aur Abu Bakr daakhil huey to unhon-ne mujhey daanta aur kaha: Shaitaan ka baaja Nabi (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) key paas? To Rasulullah (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) unki taraf mutawajjeh huey aur farmaya: Unhey chhor do. Phir jab Aap ghaafil huey to main ne unhey ishaara kya aur wo nikal gaein. (Bukhari: 949). Aisha (Raziallahu anha) se riwayat hai, unhon-ne kaha: Abu Bakr daakhil huey jabke merey paas Ansaar ki londiyon mein se do londiyaan gaa rahi thein jo Ansaar ne Buas key din kaha tha. Unhon-ne kaha: Aur wo gaaney waliyaan na thein. To Abu Bakr ne kaha: Kya shaitaan key baajey Rasulullah (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) key ghar mein, aur wo Eid key din tha. To Rasulullah (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) ne farmaya: Ae Abu Bakr! Beshak har qaum key liye Eid hai aur ye hamaari Eid hai. (952). Ye hadees Ziya-ud-Daaghistani key zawaed mein se hai aur Zabidi key asl mein se nahi hai."
"528","[AI-translation] Anas bin Maalik (Raziallahu anhu) se riwayat hai, unhon-ne kaha: Rasulullah (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) Eid-ul-Fitr key din na nikaltey yahan tak ke khajoorein kha letey. Aur aik riwayat mein hai un se: Aur unhey taaq khaatey. (Bukhari: 953)"
"529","[AI-translation] Bara bin Aazib (Raziallahu anhu) se riwayat hai, unhon-ne kaha: Main ne Rasulullah (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) ko khutba detey huey suna. To Aap ne farmaya: Beshak sab se pehla jo ham apne is din mein shuru kartey hain ye hai ke ham namaz padhein, phir wapas jaaein aur qurbaani karein. Phir jo aisa karey to beshak us ne hamaari sunnat ko paa liya. (Bukhari: 951)"
"530","[AI-translation] Aur unhi se (Bara Raziallahu anhu se) riwayat hai, unhon-ne kaha: Nabi (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) ne hamein Baqra Eid key din namaz key baad khutba diya. To farmaya: Jo hamaari namaz padhey aur hamaari qurbaani karey to beshak us ne qurbaani ko paa liya. Aur jo namaz se pehley qurbaani karey to wo namaz se pehley hai aur uskey liye qurbaani nahi hai. To Abu Burda ne jo Bara key khaalu they kaha: Ya Rasulullah! Beshak main ne namaz se pehley apni bakri qurbaan kar di aur main ne jaana ke aaj khaaney peeney ka din hai. Aur main ne chaaha ke meri bakri sab se pehli ho jo merey ghar mein zibah ki jaey. To main ne apni bakri zibah kar di aur namaz key liye aaney se pehley subah ka khaana khaaya. Aap ne farmaya: Tumhaari bakri gosht ki bakri hai. Us ne kaha: Ya Rasulullah! Beshak hamaarey paas hamaari aik saal ki bakri ka bachcha hai jo mujhey do bakriyon se zyada mehboob hai. Kya wo meri taraf se kaafi hogi? Aap ne farmaya: Haan. Aur tumharey baad kisi ki taraf se kaafi na hogi. (Bukhari: 955)"
"531","[AI-translation] Abu Saeed Khudri (Raziallahu anhu) se riwayat hai, unhon-ne kaha: Rasulullah (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) Eid-ul-Fitr aur Baqra Eid key din Eidgaah ki taraf nikaltey. To sab se pehli cheez jis se Aap shuru kartey namaz hoti. Phir Aap wapas aatey aur logon key saamney khadey hotey jabke log apni safon mein baithey hotey. To Aap unhey waaz kartey aur unhey wasiyat kartey aur unhey hukm detey. Phir agar Aap lashkar bhejna chaahtey to bhejey ya kisi cheez ka hukm dena chaahtey to hukm detey. Phir Aap wapas aatey. Abu Saeed ne kaha: To log usi par rahey yahan tak ke main Marwaan key sath nikla jabke wo Madina ka ameer tha, Baqra Eid ya Eid-ul-Fitr mein. Phir jab ham Eidgaah aey to mimbar tha jo Kaseer bin Salt ne banaaya tha. Phir Marwaan ne chaaha ke wo namaz padhney se pehley us par chadhey. To main ne uskey kapdey se kheench liya aur us ne mujhey kheencha. To wo chadha aur namaz se pehley khutba diya. To main ne us se kaha: Allah ki qasam tum ne badal diya! To us ne kaha: Ae Abu Saeed! Jo tum jaantey ho wo chala gaya. To main ne kaha: Jo main jaanta hun Allah ki qasam wo us se behtar hai jo main nahi jaanta. To us ne kaha: Beshak log namaz key baad hamaarey liye na baithey they. To main ne use namaz se pehley kar diya. (Bukhari: 956)"
"532","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas aur Jaabir bin Abdullah (Raziallahu anhum) se riwayat hai, unhon-ne kaha: Eid-ul-Fitr key din aur na Baqra Eid key din azaan kahi jaati thi. (Bukhari: 960)"
"533","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas (Raziallahu anhuma) se riwayat hai, unhon-ne kaha: Main Eid mein Rasulullah (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) aur Abu Bakr aur Umar aur Usmaan (Raziallahu anhum) key sath haazir hua. To wo sab khutbey se pehley namaz padhtey they. (Bukhari: 962)"
"534","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas (Raziallahu anhuma) se Nabi (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) se riwayat hai ke Aap ne farmaya: Dinon mein amal in (das dinon) se afzal nahi hai. Unhon-ne kaha: Aur na jihaad? Aap ne farmaya: Aur na jihaad, magar aadmi jo apni jaan aur apne maal ko khatrey mein daal kar nikley aur kisi cheez key sath wapas na aaey. (Bukhari: 969)"
"535","[AI-translation] Anas bin Maalik (Raziallahu anhu) se riwayat hai ke un se talbiya key baarey mein poochha gaya: Tum Nabi (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) key sath kaisey kartey they? Unhon-ne kaha: Talbiya kehney wala talbiya kehta, us par inkaar na kya jaata. Aur takbeer kehney wala takbeer kehta, us par inkaar na kya jaata. (Bukhari: 970)"
"536","[AI-translation] Ibn Umar (Raziallahu anhuma) se riwayat hai ke Nabi (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) Eidgaah mein oont zibah kartey ya (bakri) zibah kartey they. (Bukhari: 982)"
"537","[AI-translation] Jaabir (Raziallahu anhu) se riwayat hai, unhon-ne kaha: Nabi (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) jab Eid ka din hota to raasta badal detey. (Bukhari: 986)"
"538","[AI-translation] Aisha ne kaha: Main ne Nabi (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) ko dekha ke Aap mujhey parda kar rahey they jabke main Habsha walon ko dekh rahi thi aur wo masjid mein khel rahey they. To Umar ne unhey daanta. To Nabi (Sallallahu Alehi w aalehi wasallam) ne farmaya: Unhey chhor do. Amaan do Bani Arfida ko. (Bukhari: 988). Kitaab-ul-Witr."
